  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Sexual and Reproductive Health and Rights for Tanzanian youth and adolescents</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project aims at promoting sexual and reproductive health and rights (SRHR) for youth in Tanzania, while simultaneously building capacity in both the Danish and Tanzanian groups and advocating for gender balance, youth empowerment, and human rights. The project originated from our Pilot Project, but we will expand to rural areas in Tanzania. Through strategic activities such as school visits, speed mentoring sessions, and advocacy campaigns, we aim to empower adolescents by providing comprehensive education on SRHR, fostering community awareness and support for equality, and advocating for policy changes. By engaging stakeholders, empowering youth leaders, and promoting gender equality, our project seeks to create lasting change and improve the SRHR well-being of adolescents in our target communities.</narrative>
  </description>
